.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-pkg-upload 1  "taurctl-pkg-upload " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-pkg\-upload \- Publish or update a package from a recipe archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl pkg upload\fR [\fB\-\-org\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIARCHIVE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publish or update a package from a recipe archive.
.PP
The archive is a `.tar.gz`, `.tar`, or `.zip` with `PKGBUILD` and `.SRCINFO`. A new package is adopted by your account, or by `\-\-org` when you are an Owner, Admin, or Contributor of that organization. An update keeps the current owner. If `\-\-org` is given on an update, it must already be that package\*(Aqs organization.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fI<ORG>\fR
Organization that should own a new package. Use the exact name (3\-16 characters of A\-Z a\-z 0\-9 . _ \-, starting and ending alphanumeric). You must be an Owner, Admin, or Contributor. Omit to publish under your account. On an update, the name must already be the package\*(Aqs organization
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIARCHIVE\fR>
Path to a .tar.gz, .tar, or .zip of the package directory
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  taurctl pkg upload ./webup.tar.gz
  taurctl pkg upload ./webup.tar.gz \-\-org brains
